## Customize flags given to the VM: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erl.html
## -mode/-name/-sname/-setcookie are configured via env vars, do not set them here

## Do not cache freed memory segments. By default each allocator instance
## keeps up to ten freed segments mapped for reuse, of any size. Large process
## heaps (manifest owners, query workers) live in single-block segments of tens
## of megabytes, so the cache kept hundreds of megabytes resident that no
## allocator reported. See docs/scaling.md#memory-breakdown.
+MMmcs 0
